    "system": {
      "type": "tonescan-workflow",
      "blocks": {
        "step_tonelight": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "stats": "RGBW+IR | light channels\nABS | injection moulded\nUSB-C | power and control",
            "title": "toneLight",
            "app_icon": false,
            "body": "<p>The toneLight is our dedicated light panel designed specifically for film scanning. It features high quality red, green, and blue LED arrays picked for optimal channel separation when used with colour negative film. There is also a 95 CRI white LED panel for scanning slides or black and white film, and a 880 nm infrared one for dust reduction with compatible cameras (not yet supported in toneScan Studio).</p><p>toneLight is made to be durable and long lasting. It has a sturdy injection moulded ABS enclosure, and a machined aluminium heatsink to keep it running optimally for years of use.</p><p>All essential features can be controlled via the illuminated front buttons, and more advanced configuration and automation is available through the built-in USB-C port. The toneLight is powered by a regular USB-C Power Delivery supply, such as a phone or laptop charger, or a power bank.</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Front_panel.webp",
            "image_url": "",
            "video_url": ""
          }
        },
        "step_tonecarrier": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "stats": "3 frames | shortest film strip\n2 minutes | to scan a full roll\n5 minutes | to upgrade",
            "title": "toneCarrier",
            "app_icon": false,
            "body": "<p>Two years ago we launched the toneCarrier as a robust, low cost film carrier for 35 mm and 120 film. Today it is trusted by thousands of photographers all around the world. Building on this solid foundation, we developed a motorised version which can automatically feed and move film along to make automatic scanning possible.</p><p>toneCarrier uses a unique dual roller belt drive system that makes it possible to scan even short strips of film (3 frames of 35 mm). Flatness is achieved by a dual s-curve film channel, which applies gentle tension to the film without any contact with the emulsion.</p><p><strong>All existing toneCarriers can be upgraded to the motorised version in less than 5 minutes.</strong> It's the same toneCarrier you may already know and use, but even faster and easier to use. The motor upgrade is fully compatible with our manual carriers and needs minimal disassembly.</p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Showcase_HD.webp",
            "image_url": "",
            "video_url": ""
          }
        },
        "step_tonescan": {
          "type": "step",
          "settings": {
            "title": "toneScan Studio",
            "stats": "[mac] [windows] | macOS and Windows",
            "badge": "Open beta",
            "app_icon": true,
            "body": "<p>toneScan Studio is our standalone desktop software made to work with the RGB scanning system. It automatically handles the capture, merging, and inversion of trichrome scans. It also supports scans made with white light, as well as slides and black and white film.</p><p>It uses an advanced inversion engine which emulates a real darkroom print. With smart automatic corrections and default settings, the scans are usually usable with no additional corrections. And if you do want to change something, the GPU accelerated viewport and 1:1 pixel perfect previews make it quick and precise.</p><p>toneScan Studio integrates seamlessly with our hardware. For RGB scans, it automatically calibrates the light settings before each session, ensuring great and consistent results every time.</p><p><a href=\"/pages/tonescan\" title=\"toneScan Studio\">Explore toneScan Studio →</a></p>",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Edit_viewport.webp",
            "image_url": "",
            "video_url": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "step_tonelight",
        "step_tonecarrier",
        "step_tonescan"
      ],
      "settings": {
        "eyebrow": "",
        "heading": "What makes toneScan special?",
        "subheading": "We built a system that allows you to replicate time-proven lab scanner techniques with your standard camera-based scanning rig.",
        "keep_dark": true
      }
    },
