        "review_7": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "I'm very impressed with the toneCarrier 120 Mark II. The kit is well made and, most importantly, it does an excellent job of keeping my film flat while scanning. I've previously used a much more expensive holder from Negative Supply and, honestly, I prefer this. It may not be machined from aluminium, but it's easier to load film into and gives better results in terms of flatness. The only thing worth mentioning is that I initially had a little trouble attaching the Easyloader tray and Auto-spooling catch trays. The tabs needed careful alignment when sliding into the slots and caught slightly the first couple of times I tried. Probably a rough edge or something as it's been absolutely fine ever since. Overall, this is an excellent scanning kit and I'd highly recommend it.",
            "author": "Graeme",
            "product": "toneCarrier 120 kit (Mark II)",
            "date": "May 2026",
            "source": "Etsy"
          }
        },
        "review_8": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "Great product with quality build. I bought the 120 film version and will buy the 35mm version next.",
            "author": "David",
            "product": "toneCarrier 120 kit (Mark II)",
            "date": "April 2026",
            "source": "Etsy"
          }
        },
        "review_9": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "This was very well put together and it prints to perfection, once put together it scans my negatives flawlessly!",
            "author": "Javier E.",
            "product": "toneCarrier 120 (STL)",
            "date": "April 2026",
            "source": "tonephotographic.com"
          }
        },
        "review_10": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "I cannot fault this thing. Printed and assembled from the studio, supplied with very clear instruction on print settings and assembly. The Tone carrier has given me faith in achieving high quality digital output, without the need for lab services.",
