          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "Flawless handling and really well made, congratulations on this product, thought through down to the last detail.",
            "author": "Hendrick",
            "product": "toneCarrier 35 mm kit (Mark II)",
            "date": "November 2025",
            "source": "Etsy"
          }
        },
        "review_16": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "I’m really into 3D printing and DIY projects, so I bought the STL files along with the hardware kit. I printed everything on my Bambu Lab A1 mini (yes, it’s possible to print it on a 180x180 plate, you just need to rotate most parts by 45° and slice them yourself). I used a high-quality print profile, and the results turned out great. 👌 After some time using it, I accidentally broke a part, but I just printed a new one. That’s one of the best parts of this setup - infinite repairability through 3D printing. I highly recommend getting the full scanning kit, since the easy loader and catch trays work beautifully. The whole scanning process is easy and feels smooth. I also really enjoy how the film advances using the knobs - super satisfying! As for film flatness, it’s pretty good overall. I only notice slight issues on the first or last frame of a roll, which seems to be common with most film holders. I haven’t compared it to others, but I’ve heard people report similar (or worse) flatness problems even on higher-end models like the VALOI Easy 120. Great product, 100% recommend! 😄",
            "author": "Pawel",
            "product": "toneCarrier 120 kit (STL)",
            "date": "November 2025",
            "source": "tonephotographic.com"
          }
        },
        "review_17": {
          "type": "review",
          "settings": {
            "stars": 5,
            "text": "This holder keeps 120 film absolutely flat — exactly what I needed for high-quality scans. Build quality is great, and customer service was outstanding. Strongly recommend!",
            "author": "Lena",
            "product": "toneCarrier 120 holder (Mark II)",
            "date": "September 2025",
